\ The entry file imports `probe` from module A while module B exports a
\ colliding `probe`. `e-quot` is an entry-file word handing out a stored
\ quotation kept uncompilable by its nested definition, so the quotation
\ runs interpreted inside the runtime image with no defining module. Its
\ bare `probe` must resolve through the entry's restored durable import
\ frame, deterministically landing on A's export instead of scanning the
\ module cache by name.

use { probe: } "fixtures/own_module_image_entry_a.1z" ;
use { b-tag: } "fixtures/own_module_image_entry_b.1z" ;

e-quot: ( -- q ) [ [ inner: [ probe ] ; inner ] ] ;

probe print-line
e-quot call print-line
b-tag print-line
